#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087450 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "446ea007-1ff4-5023-8e3f-7f00eb0fb2d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-5071" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/848/Source/Images/e5e3e1baad54a5ce65047fbcb5e7a58d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=5$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3$. Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}} + \\frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{5^{2}} + \\frac{y^{2}}{3^{2}} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{25} + \\frac{y^{2}}{9} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087451 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "af56117c-65e0-5f12-9780-7a95e6be829e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5072" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/848/Source/Images/10eddd924b3dc68fbf1bb4eaeb8f92c5.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4$. Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}} + \\frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{2^{2}} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4^{2}} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{16} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087452 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "b7c94673-f847-5977-9b9f-8d235ea42eb2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5073" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation $\\dfrac{x^2}{36} + \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1$?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nIn the given equation, we have $a^2=36$ and $b^2=25$.\n\n- Since $a^2=36$, the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36} = 6$.\n- Since $b^2=25$, the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25} = 5$.\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=6$, and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5$.\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length\n\n$$\n2a = 2 \\cdot 6 = 12\n$$\n\nand the minor axis has length\n\n$$\n2b = 2 \\cdot 5 =10\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23cd513c-0f75-5c1f-b46c-45e80c3719c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267447} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7d5c88-1459-536c-b6da-74258ee639fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267448} {:answer/id #uuid "2da80e4f-bebd-5d21-bbbf-0441a5bd9e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267449} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd22e77-097f-5aed-a9f0-69d727c4148f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267450} {:answer/id #uuid "da0b1065-0ffd-54b2-a18a-78cfcc4ec9da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bd22e77-097f-5aed-a9f0-69d727c4148f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267450} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb2af5e-054b-59f7-be64-d428bf579b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20f799f9-37ea-5b3e-b820-5abed8180539" :question/math-academy-id "q-16451" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/6116ecf00a26d9828b238879b61385c1296f33ff863dbb8337a3b22be5981f10.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec17315-ecea-5a46-86b9-10826fc86f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267493} {:answer/id #uuid "709bd1aa-6289-5f10-a063-81c1ac15b7ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267494} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc5aca1-cf29-5761-be5f-7bdf0e50b9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267495} {:answer/id #uuid "3f96ca79-5e37-5709-a2c2-fb41f6a9e901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267496} {:answer/id #uuid "4c823ea5-1ab4-51c8-9be9-6254583d5542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bc5aca1-cf29-5761-be5f-7bdf0e50b9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267495} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ab01a51-dea6-54fe-8d4a-a18973f2a125" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75a4ea63-60ed-555d-b33c-9e409712e1e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73619" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/8637901efc126236b190e7012cf65a06be078cb21c3093eff39b927493000138.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1.5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{2}^{2}})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{9}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81292d50-5c51-5b38-89f0-949bc6b6a964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{8} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086540} {:answer/id #uuid "0c18f3df-95fb-536c-8e2f-3029a38b2427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086541} {:answer/id #uuid "1e67014b-0d00-54c0-af93-fd3ae84e9b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086542} {:answer/id #uuid "3c28a557-2851-503b-97be-c5d293379692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{16} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086543} {:answer/id #uuid "7affd3de-ff29-5c52-853b-6c179253ff99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{16} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7affd3de-ff29-5c52-853b-6c179253ff99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{16} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086544} :answer-field/id #uuid "92982adf-0bda-5979-982f-53887542631a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "808bb938-3f2e-5c94-82a4-205181f5d6ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-7604" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/848/Source/Images/q-7604.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=4$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
